For a locally small category C, the hom functor is the functor
\hom _C : C^{\text {op}} \times C \to \text {Set}
from the product category of the opposite category of C and C into the category of sets \text {Set}.

A presheaf on a small category C is a functor
F : C^{\text {op}} \to \text {Set}
from the opposite category of C to the category of sets. Similar to category of functors, we can define the category of presheaves on C, denoted \text {Set}^{C^{\text {op}}}.

